From a6fadcf93939c6c0a2b27542bb2245f327eace65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:30:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: guest PC sampling profiler (PS2X_PC_SAMPLE)

When PS2X_PC_SAMPLE=<path.csv> is set, EeScheduler::reset starts a host thread that samples at ~1 kHz the pc of the guest context the EE executor is running (std::atomic_ref relaxed read of ctx->pc, racy by design), the guest thread id, the vsync tick, and four section flags: vu1 (VU1Interpreter::run), iop (IOP RPC, SIF transfer, runEeCycles), gs (PCSX2 gifPacket from the GIF arbiter), gsvsync (PCSX2 vsync + snapshot at VBlankStart). The CSV "tick,tid,pc,count,vu1,iop,gs,gsvsync" has one row per (64-tick bucket, thread, pc); pc 0 = executor outside guest code. Rewritten every ~2 s (tmp + rename) and at the end of run(), so a killed run loses at most 2 s. Unset: no thread, one bool load per flag site.
